---
// One calculator per compound. The arithmetic is the same on every one of these
// pages, so the arithmetic is not what makes them different: the doses that
// published studies of that compound actually used are, and those are quoted
// from the record with their evidence tier and their source.
//
// Nothing here takes a body weight or a condition, and nothing returns a dose.
// Showing what a trial administered is reporting, which is what the whole site
// does; suggesting what a reader should take would be advice, which it never does.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Calculators from '../../components/Calculators.astro';
import Tier from '../../components/v2/Tier.astro';
import { records } from '../../lib/collections';
import { qualifies, doseRows, humanDoseRows, doseFigures } from '../../lib/calculators';
import { isIndexable, TIER_LABEL } from '../../lib/site';

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const compounds = await records('compounds');
  return compounds.filter(qualifies).map((entry) => ({
    params: { slug: entry.data.slug },
    props: { entry },
  }));
}
const { entry } = Astro.props;
const d = entry.data as any;
const name = d.preferred_name;
const path = `/calculators/${d.slug}`;
const rows = doseRows(entry);
const human = humanDoseRows(entry);
const figures = doseFigures(entry);
const sources = new Map<string, any>((d.sources ?? []).map((s: any) => [s.id, s]));
const routes = (d.attributes?.routes_studied ?? []) as any[];

const title = `${name} Dosage Calculator: mg to mL and Syringe Units`;
const description = `Convert ${name} vial mass and diluent into concentration, draw volume and syringe units, beside the doses published studies of ${name} actually used, each one cited.`;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} indexable={isIndexable(entry)} siteSuffix={false}>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/calculators">Calculators</a></p>
    <h1>{name} dosage calculator</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      The arithmetic is the same for every peptide, so the part worth reading is underneath it:
      the {human.length > 0 ? 'doses' : 'figures'} that published studies of {name} actually used,
      quoted and tiered. This tool converts the numbers you enter. It does not suggest what to take.
    </p>

    <Calculators slug="reconstitution-calculator" />

    <h2 id="studied">Doses in published studies of {name}</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Every row is quoted from a paper in this compound's own source ledger and carries the kind of
      evidence it came from. {human.length === 0
        ? `None of them is a human dose: no study in this ledger administered ${name} to people at a stated dose. Animal figures are given per kilogram of animal and do not convert to a person by arithmetic.`
        : `${human.length} of ${rows.length} come from human studies. The rest are animal or laboratory work, where a per-kilogram figure does not convert to a person.`}
    </p>
    <div class="card clip"><div class="tblwrap"><table class="tbl">
      <caption>What studies of {name} administered, as published. Not a recommendation and not a range to pick from.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">Dose as the paper states it</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td><Tier tier={r.tier} /></td>
            <td>{r.value}</td>
            <td>{r.sourceIds.map((id) => {
              const s = sources.get(id);
              return s?.url
                ? <a href={s.url} rel="nofollow noopener">{id}</a>
                : <span>{id}</span>;
            })}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table></div></div>

    {routes.length > 0 && (
      <Fragment>
        <h2 id="routes">How {name} was given in those studies</h2>
        <p class="prose">The route changes what a dose means. A figure from an intravenous infusion is not the same quantity as the same number given under the skin.</p>
        <ul class="list">{routes.slice(0, 6).map((r: any) => <li>{r.value}</li>)}</ul>
      </Fragment>
    )}

    <h2 id="refuses">What this calculator will not do</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      It will not take a body weight and return a milligram figure. That is a clinical decision, not
      a division: it depends on why someone is taking something, what else they take, and what their
      kidneys and liver are doing. None of that is knowable from a number typed into a box.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      The table above is the published record, not a menu. {human.length === 0
        ? `For ${name} in particular, there is no human dose in this ledger to copy even if you wanted to.`
        : `A dose that appeared in a trial appeared under supervision, with monitoring, in people selected to be in that trial.`}
      The full evidence, including what was measured and what went wrong, is on the <a href={`/compounds/${d.slug}`}>{name} record</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="other">Other calculators</h2>
    <ul class="cards">
      <li><a href="/tools/reconstitution-calculator">Generic reconstitution calculator</a><div class="sub">The same arithmetic, without a compound attached</div></li>
      <li><a href="/tools/unit-converter">Unit converter</a><div class="sub">mg, mcg, ng and syringe units</div></li>
      <li><a href="/tools/vial-planner">Vial planner</a><div class="sub">How many draws a vial yields and how long it lasts</div></li>
      <li><a href="/calculators">All compound calculators</a><div class="sub">Every compound with published dose figures</div></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
